.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt TCPDUMP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm tcpdump
.Nd decode and filter classic pcap capture files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl nnStv
.Op Fl c Ar count
.Op Fl i Ar interface
.Op Fl r Ar file
.Op Fl w Ar file
.Op Ar filter
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a classic pcap savefile and prints one line per packet in the format used
by the K277 fixture matrix.
It decodes Ethernet II, ARP, IPv4, IPv6, TCP, UDP, ICMPv4 and ICMPv6, including
the DNS query/answer subset on ports 53 and 5353.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar count
Stop after
.Ar count
packets that pass the filter.
.It Fl i Ar interface
Select a live capture interface.
This userspace build has no BPF capture device, so
.Fl i
is rejected with a clear error; use
.Fl r .
.It Fl n , Fl nn
Print numeric addresses and ports.
This is the only implemented mode.
.It Fl r Ar file
Read
.Ar file
as a classic pcap savefile.
.It Fl S
Print absolute TCP sequence numbers instead of sequence numbers relative to
the initial sequence number observed in the capture.
.It Fl t , Fl tt
With
.Fl t
suppress the timestamp; with
.Fl tt
print seconds since the Unix epoch and the savefile fraction.
.It Fl v , Fl vv
Print the verbose IP header and IPv4 header-checksum marker.
.Fl vv
also prints TCP sequence numbers for empty segments.
.It Fl w Ar file
Write the packets that pass the filter as a little-endian classic pcap.
.El
.Pp
The trailing
.Ar filter
is a BPF-style expression.
The supported grammar is documented in
.Pa docs/tcpdump.md :
protocol primitives
.Pq tcp , udp , icmp , icmp6 , ip , ip6 , arp ,
.Cm host
and
.Cm port
qualifiers,
.Cm and , or , not ,
and protocol-relative byte tests such as
.Li tcp[tcpflags] & tcp-syn != 0
or
.Li ip[6:2] & 0x1fff != 0 .
.Pp
A malformed savefile, an unsupported link type or a filter that does not
compile is an error and the tool exits non-zero.
A packet with a bad IPv4 header checksum is decoded with a visible
.Dq bad cksum
marker in verbose mode.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 1 ,
.Xr netstat 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
